Leapmotor cloud client (real car data, optional):
  This product includes code ported from LMB10 (https://github.com/txurtxil/LPB10) by txurtxil,
  licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 and combined with Qonecta+ under section 13
  of both licenses. Only the protocol part was ported (login, session refresh, request signing, vehicle
  list and status); none of LMB10's remote-control functions.
    app/src/main/java/com/headqlink/link/LeapCrypto.java  - signing, HKDF key, account PKCS#12 password, device id
    app/src/main/java/com/headqlink/link/LeapApi.java     - login, session, token refresh, vehicle list and status
    app/src/main/java/com/headqlink/link/LeapStatus.java  - signal table, field merging, conversions, charge/tyre rules
  The unofficial Leapmotor API may stop working at any time. Qonecta+ is not affiliated with Leapmotor.

Range-extender (REEV) signals and the Leapmotor cloud trip history:
  The fuel signals (3235 tank %, 3263 millilitres, 3259 fuel range, 3261 total range) and the
  per-trip history fields (routeStartTs, routeEndTs, totalMileage, totalEnergy, driveReevOil) follow
  leapmotor-mate (https://github.com/ProtossBlaster/leapmotor-mate) by ProtossBlaster; the weekly
  consumption endpoint follows leapmotor-api (https://github.com/markoceri/leapmotor-api) by markoceri.
  Both are licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0. No code was copied; Qonecta+
  reimplements the read-only requests in LeapApi.java, LeapStatus.java and CloudHistory.java.
  The only commands to the car are the opt-in ones of the "Car" widget (lock, unlock, boot, climate and
  find; sent only if the user saves the car PIN and turns them on). They follow leapmotor-api's flow
  (certificate sync, AES-encrypted PIN verify, remote/ctl with cmdId 110, 120, 130 and 170, result query),
  reimplemented in LeapApi.remote() and LeapCrypto.operatePassword(). No other remote command exists.

Charging point data (Route tab and charge plan):
  In Spain, chargers come from the official registry of public charging points of the Ministry for the
  Ecological Transition (MITECO), published by the DGT on Spain's National Access Point (nap.dgt.es,
  DATEX II "electrolineras" publication) under a Creative Commons Attribution licence. Qonecta+
  downloads it on the phone at most once a week and keeps a compact copy (DgtChargers.java). Elsewhere,
  and for points missing from the registry, chargers come from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap
  contributors, ODbL) through the public Overpass servers.

Maps, routes, search, weather and elevation (online services the app queries):
  Map data (C) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright): map tiles from
  tile.openstreetmap.org, roads, speed limits and chargers through the public Overpass servers, routes
  from the OSRM demo server (https://project-osrm.org), place search with Photon by komoot
  (https://photon.komoot.io) and Nominatim (https://nominatim.org).
  Weather data and elevation by Open-Meteo.com (https://open-meteo.com), CC BY 4.0; elevation fallback
  from Open Topo Data (https://www.opentopodata.org) with NASA SRTM data.
  Ad and tracker blocking (web browser and TV web channels): the domain list "HaGeZi Pro mini" from HaGeZi's DNS
  blocklists (https://github.com/hagezi/dns-blocklists, GPL-3.0), downloaded by the app once a week; not bundled.
  Internet radio directory: radio-browser.info (https://www.radio-browser.info). TV lists: the app reads the
  TDTChannels list format (https://github.com/LaQuay/TDTChannels, Apache-2.0); no list is bundled.
  Road guide: place summaries and photos from Wikipedia (https://www.wikipedia.org, text under CC BY-SA 4.0) and
  Wikimedia Commons (each photo under its own free licence), fetched while the guide is open; not bundled. The app
  shows them with the source; summaries are shortened (without parentheses or references).
  Karaoke: song lyrics from LRCLIB (https://lrclib.net), fetched on demand for the song that is playing and kept only
  in memory; not bundled. The lyrics belong to their authors.

