Super Nintendo emulator (Games > SNES, the user's own ROM files):
  The core is bsnes by byuu and contributors (libretro port, https://github.com/libretro/bsnes, based on
  https://github.com/bsnes-emu/bsnes), copied into app/src/main/cpp/bsnes: bsnes is licensed under the GNU General
  Public License version 3 (LICENSE.txt, GPLv3.txt there), nall and libco under the ISC license, and the Game Boy core
  used for the Super Game Boy (bsnes/gb, SameBoy by Lior Halphon) under the MIT license. It is combined with Qonecta+
  under section 13 of the AGPL v3. The only change is the audio rate in target-libretro/libretro.cpp (44100 Hz instead
  of 48000); see bsnes/UPSTREAM.md. app/src/main/cpp/hql_snes.cpp is Qonecta+'s own minimal libretro frontend.
  Qonecta+ ships no game ROMs. Nintendo, Super Nintendo and SNES are trademarks of Nintendo; Qonecta+ is not
  affiliated with Nintendo.

PlayStation emulator (Games > PS1, the user's own disc images):
  The core is PCSX ReARMed by notaz and contributors (libretro port, https://github.com/libretro/pcsx_rearmed), based
  on PCSX-Reloaded and PCSX, with the psx_gpu NEON renderer by Exophase and the dfsound SPU by Pete Bernert and
  contributors, copied into app/src/main/cpp/pcsx_rearmed. It is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2
  or (at your option) any later version (COPYING there) and is used here under version 3, combined with Qonecta+ under
  section 13 of the AGPL v3. It includes libchdr (BSD 3-clause), the LZMA SDK (public domain), zstd (BSD) and
  libretro-common (MIT). The code is unmodified; see pcsx_rearmed/UPSTREAM.md. app/src/main/cpp/hql_psx.cpp is
  Qonecta+'s own minimal libretro frontend. No Sony BIOS is shipped: the core uses its own high-level BIOS emulation
  unless the user provides one. Qonecta+ ships no games. PlayStation and PS1 are trademarks of Sony Interactive
  Entertainment; Qonecta+ is not affiliated with Sony.

